    {
      "id": "8bd1187b-5b3c-4a3c-bbf8-5a5534ed9469",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -560,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 816,
        "content": "## Human-approved Instagram posts\n\n### How it works\n\n1. A protected form collects an image and verified facts.\n2. Gemini drafts a caption from those inputs.\n3. Code checks the caption and builds five hashtags.\n4. A reviewer approves or rejects through a Telegram link.\n5. Instagram publishes approved drafts; Telegram reports the outcome.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Connect Basic Auth to the submission form.\n- [ ] Connect Google Gemini credentials to the drafting node.\n- [ ] Connect a bot credential to every Telegram node.\n- [ ] Connect Facebook Graph API credentials to every Meta node; use a linked Instagram professional account with publishing access.\n- [ ] Set Instagram account ID, Telegram chat ID, and brand values in Configure Brand and Channels.\n- [ ] Test with a public JPEG. Reject first, then approve a separate real publishing test.\n- [ ] Activate the workflow and use the production form URL.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust language, voice, hashtags, and confidence in the configuration node. Keep approval links private."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
